socket2 0.5.10: TCP keep-alive idle time on QNX 8

socket2 0.5 imports libc::TCP_KEEPALIVE for every QNX, but libc 0.2.186
(the last release that knows target_env "nto80", see the recipe) defines it
only for QNX 7: "unresolved import libc::TCP_KEEPALIVE". QNX 8's io-sock is
the FreeBSD stack: use TCP_KEEPIDLE (256, <netinet/tcp.h>) in seconds there,
as for the BSDs; TCP_KEEPALIVE with a struct timeval stays for QNX 7.
Applied after socket2-0.5.10-qnx-ipv6-multicast.patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [libc crate gap for target_env nto80]
